From 4b53e94c076918258ed4cd46add2a9b29edb078f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harvey Bellini <harveybellini@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:37:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] S11: quick hardening for logs, prompts, retries, and
 backups

F13: the SQS parse-failure log now names only the message id and error type. F15: the frontend retries idempotent verbs only, so a lost POST cannot duplicate a run. F16: time_zone must be IANA and at most 64 characters, place labels are capped at 200, and prompt interpolation collapses and caps both. F17/F12: proposal rejections carry a bounded RejectionCode for prompts, exceptions, and logs while the tool response keeps the specific detail; route failures log a hashed place pair. F18: DynamoDB point-in-time recovery is on. F20: published MCP configs contain no owner paths.
